{"title":"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In multiplying two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, Ron reversed the digits of the two-digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. His erroneous product was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a141918ea2696454645ae9d426e11ef432dcdc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$161.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> What is the correct value of the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4aaa78a0e23075ae3c86cc71856c75d72925d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 116 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 161 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 204 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 214 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"440\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8403aaee7e752f7fadd7a9beb7ba81262bd41a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$161$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> reveals that it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/90604f5ad990860da03b23ea8679fe0b9013f47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23*7.$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> Therefore, the only ways to represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8403aaee7e752f7fadd7a9beb7ba81262bd41a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$161$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> as a product of two positive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3780818ac27d9aeda27eb0a3a93fce7cb429e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$161*1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/90604f5ad990860da03b23ea8679fe0b9013f47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23*7.$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> Because neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8403aaee7e752f7fadd7a9beb7ba81262bd41a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$161$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a two-digit number, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17ce6fcb2994d4241d780dd5311d828db133411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a two-digit number, we know that a, with its two digits reversed, gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9803b67b315db7dfce1c1ce717cfaaa8ec4d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e07a77fbd1dfd66033443e1917e56cc7cd142b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 32$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbfa1f272b20123aa84aa230975d60d0f36f685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7.$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> Multiplying our two correct values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> yields\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b15af41adbaac2f450d801429ad90374b7824b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a*b = 32*7 =\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2565fe98537a4d80d87df8cc8475c4e2d9b00ab6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\boxed{224 \\textbf{(E)}}\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B\">2011 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflin